  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Youth Energy Hackathon in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supported innovative solutions to reduce diesel dependence on Gili Ketapang island, where electricity generation largely relies on diesel. Through the Youth Energy Hackathon 2025, initiated by the Dutch Embassy in Indonesia and Energy Academy Indonesia (ECADIN), more than 500 teams were invited to develop reliable, affordable and sustainable energy solutions, contributing to Indonesia&#x2019;s Net Zero Emission ambitions.Participants received mentoring from Dutch companies, and one winning team was selected to further develop and test its solution on site. The team installed solar panels, floating solar panels on fish cages, and a battery energy storage system connected to a hydrogen facility. The resulting system now provides sustainable electricity for approximately six hours per day for the entire island. The project also supported local livelihoods by training women to operate the solar systems and by developing a digital marketplace tool to expand the sales of locally produced fish crackers to other islands.</narrative>
  </description>
